{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>From upon the altar.</b> The outer one." "<b>From before YHWH.</b> From the side that is in front of the entrance — and that is the western side." "<b>Fine.</b> Why does Scripture say דַּקָּה? But is not all the incense fine, as it says ״וְשָׁחַקְתָּ מִמֶּנָּה הָדֵק״ (Exodus 36)? Rather, that it be fine beyond fine — for on the eve of Yom HaKippurim he would return it to the mortar (Keritot 6)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:45.090012079Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}